There is no one way to do it because models should be built on a priori understanding of the system. Many researchers start with determining p while fixing all three parameters global - psi, gamma, and epsilon. Then feeding the best p model to determine psi, still keeping gamma and epsilon global, and subsequently determining epsilon and gamma in the next steps using the same logic.

John shared a really good paper discussing different modeling strategies and how they impact your inferences. A must-read.

